WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.367
-Margot, you're very, very nice.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.968
What did you -- What did you bring me tonight?

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:07.934
-This is an Australian delicacy called fairy bread

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:11.334
typically served at young children's birthday parties

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.734
where I'm from.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:15.000
And since it's your birthday, Jimmy...

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.067
-Yeah, it is my birthday. Yeah, of course.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.868
[ Cheers and applause ] -I mean...

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.334
I think we should sing Jimmy "Happy Birthday."

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.400
-Oh, my goodness. -100%. Don't you think?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.400
-Alright. -Okay.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.300
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.634
-Thank you very much.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:36.868
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.000
-You're amazing.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.734
-♪ Happy birthday, dear Jimmy ♪

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.767
-I appreciate it.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:51.234
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:54.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.000
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.067
That is so thoughtful and nice.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.567
I want to make this about you, not about me tonight.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.834
But I'm going have a bite of the -- What is fairy bread?

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:07.934
-Fairy bread is white bread -- the cheaper the better --

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.400
butter, and then sprinkles on top.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.334
-Oh, it's fantastic. -And it's great.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.300
If you haven't tried it, I highly recommend it.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.634
-It's good luck. -Don't even wait

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.234
for your birthday. Just have it any time.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.801
-Just have it. Fairy bread. Any time.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:21.167
New York is kind of a second home for you.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.701
-Yes. -Because --

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.567
-It's the first place I lived when I moved to America.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:25.934
-Really? -Yeah.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.367
-Where did you live in New York? -I was living in Brooklyn.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.567
I was in South Williamsburg,

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.200
and then I lived in Bed-Stuy for a little bit.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.234
And then I was in -- close to Union Square.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.133
-No way. -Yeah.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.567
-So when you come home, you're like,

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:38.067
"Oh, yeah, I know this place."

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:40.234
-Yeah, it's so -- I came back, and I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.033
I want to live here again. I love it so much."

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.801
-Yeah. I read somewhere, one of the most --

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.734
things that you were excited about seeing

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:49.501
when you come to the States is red Solo cups.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.400
-Yes. -That's very interesting.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.300
-I have to tell you, as an Australian --

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.501
and probably, you know, a lot of, you know,

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.901
people from other countries -- you come to America,

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:01.968
and you realize that all the things you've seen in a movie

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.667
are actually true.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.200
[ Laughter ] Like, I was astounded.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.100
Like, I was like, "Oh, they really do have the grates

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.901
on the sidewalk that, like, blow up steam."

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:12.300
And the cabs are all yellow. -Yeah.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.868
-And, like, people do get mad

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.534
when you walk slowly on the sidewalk.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.734
Like, I just -- Everything was so exciting.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.567
And it was just like in the movies.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:22.334
And the thing I got so excited about

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:25.901
that I had always seen in movies was red Solo cups at parties.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.033
And that, we don't have that in Australia.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:31.901
I don't know why. I -- And that was so thrilling.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.167
And when I would go back to Australia,

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:35.834
literally my friends were like,

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.434
"Can you please bring some red Solo cups?

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:39.767
Because we have a party coming up, and it would be so cool."

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.634
-So your luggage is filled with red Solo cups.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:44.300
-No, I would have, like, half a suitcase of red Solo cups.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.400
I don't know why someone's not just importing them

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.634
because it would be -- Yeah, go gangbusters.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.901
-Your pal Ryan Gosling was here.

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:53.334
I know he's in the "Barbie" movie with you.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:56.200
And, by the way, he said you're hilarious.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.734
And he was telling me. I said, "Oh, we love it."

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:01.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:03.167
This movie is going to crush.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.467
-I can't tell you how mortified we were, by the way.

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:07.100
We look like we're, like, laughing, having fun,

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.400
but dying on the inside.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.734
-You're like, "Oh, my. Oh." -Dying.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.100
-You look so cool. -I was like, "This is the most

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.968
humiliating moment of my life." -Yeah.

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:16.133
Did you realize it was going to go everywhere,

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.501
all over the Internet? -No.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.434
I mean, I knew that we had some exteriors

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.234
to shoot in L.A.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.901
I knew, okay, once you're doing exteriors,

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.167
you're gonna get papped.

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.033
There's probably going to be a little crowd of people

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.834
who are going to take notice because, you know, the fluoro.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.901
We stand out a little in those outfits.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.267
-You think? Yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.534
-And so I knew there would be a little bit of attention

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:36.801
and probably some photos would get out there,

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.601
but not like it did.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:41.067
It was, like, mad. -Yeah.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.200
-It was, like, hundreds of people watching.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.968
-He said you were so funny in this

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.300
and you're so fun to work with.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.501
-He's so funny in this. -Yeah.

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.033
I want to talk about "Amsterdam," though.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.934
-Oh, my gosh. Yes. -Oh, my gosh. David O. Russell.

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.501
I mean, you can't get better than that.

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:53.868
-I mean, just try and list

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.367
the cast members that are in this film.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.300
-Christian Bale. -There's too many.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.901
-Robert De Niro. -Zoe Saldana, Anya Taylor-joy.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.834
Rami Malek. Matthias Schoenaerts.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:04.634
-Oh, everybody. -Andrea Riseborough.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:05.901
John David Washington.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.534
I mean, Mike Myers. Michael Shannon.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.033
-Chris Rock is fantastic in this.

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:11.400
-Could go on forever. There's so many.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.901
-Yeah. How is it working with David O. Russell?

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:17.667
-Oh, my gosh. Every day is like a complete --

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.067
No day is the same.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.334
-You told me that he almost doesn't ever want to stop.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:24.033
-No, he doesn't want to stop. Like, he could go forever.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.601
And same with Christian, who's, you know, the lead in this film.

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:28.601
Christian Bale plays this incredible character

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.434
and is also a very, very, you know, incredible actor.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:34.868
And they're both so dedicated to this film and their craft

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:39.000
that we never actually -- Like, he never called "cut."

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.167
David never called cut on this film.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.200
So, technically, we didn't ever really stop.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.667
-You're still filming "Amsterdam."

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.367
-We're still going.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.300
-You're still filming, and the movie's out.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.667
-It'll be in theaters October 7th, but we are still --

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:53.300
-But, no, we were there, and it was the last day of shooting,

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.067
and it was a scene and Christian was, you know, giving --

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:58.767
saying his dialogue.

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:01.834
And David's there, and he's directing.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.167
Chivo, our incredible cinematographer,

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:05.868
is filming and everyone's in it.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.200
But the permit -- You know, the curfew was up.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.701
You know, you get a permit to shoot somewhere.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:11.968
-Yeah.

00:05:11.968 --> 00:05:13.634
-We were in Pasadena, and the time was up.

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:16.067
-Yeah, of course. -And we were meant to clear out, but we wouldn't.

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:17.434
And the producers are freaking out,

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:20.234
and David's still going and Christian's still acting.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.434
And then, eventually, like, the Pasadena police

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:25.400
literally were, like, in the set with us

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.300
all being like, "Stop. You have to stop.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.667
Like, you guys have to stop. Like, please."

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.067
-The police wrapped this film.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:34.667
-The police literally -- And I could see this policewoman

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.067
trying to think of --

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:38.100
I could see her head being like, "What is the word

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.400
they use in the film business to make everything stop?"

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.734
And she was like, "Enough! Like, stop! Everyone, stop!"

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:45.100
And then she was like, "Wrap! Wrap!

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.000
You're wrapped! Everyone's wrapped!"

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.267
-That's a wrap!

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:49.801
-And, honestly, everyone heard the word "wrap,"

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.701
put down the equipment, and started packing up.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.334
-"Respect. Take care." -And I was like,

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:55.801
"Wow. A policewoman from Pasadena

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:58.634
just wrapped this film." It was incredible.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:02.200
-It's a fascinating movie. -Yeah.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.300
-And based on a true story.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.000
-So, based on a lot of true things that happened.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.501
There's a big --

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:12.133
There's a lot of unknown history that is quite astounding

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:15.300
that David and Christian explored a lot, and you see --

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.934
You find out a lot of it in the movie,

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:19.067
but really it's a big --

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:22.167
It's, like, an epic comedic thriller.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.267
It's these three -- You follow these three friends

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:26.701
who kind of get caught up

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:28.501
in this murder-mystery conspiracy

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:30.534
and a larger conspiracy, but it's really about, you know,

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:34.734
love and friendship and loyalty. It's very funny.

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.868
-It's a good story. It's very funny, very -- Yeah.

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:39.234
And, like you said, you can't name a better --

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:40.467
All this cast. -Yeah.

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:42.267
-Oh, my gosh. -The cast is incredible.

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:43.701
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:45.300
Here's Margot Robbie in "Amsterdam."

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.534
Take a look at this.

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:48.734
-I never expected two decorated soldiers

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:51.400
to get knocked out in my own home.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.734
-No. Just one, sir.

00:06:53.734 --> 00:06:57.300
-Oh, that's right, Mr. Woodman. You were too fast for Carlton.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:58.868
-I was.

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:01.767
-They started talking to Valerie, and she's not well.

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:05.701
And please, darling girl, stop crying.

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.801
-It's only natural for her to cry.

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:11.033
She just found out her friend is dead.

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:13.801
We couldn't keep it from her for forever.

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:16.667
-I'm not so ill that I can't talk to people.

00:07:16.667 --> 00:07:19.133
-You leave me here with this invalid when you know very well

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:20.801
that I think she should be hospitalized.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:22.100
It's for her own good.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.400
-Don't you ever say that to me again.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.801
-I can't handle -- -I'll put you in a hospital!

00:07:25.801 --> 00:07:26.901
I'll send you to a witch trial!

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:29.934
-Please! Please! Ladies! Stop.

00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:35.133
I'm sorry. I'm sorry I had to raise my voice.

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:38.000
-Yeah. Margot Robbie, everybody.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.801
"Amsterdam" hits theaters October 7th.

